{{also|wurgen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|würgen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|wurgen}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*wurgijaną}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*werǵʰ-|t=bind, squeeze}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|wurgen}}, {{m|nl|worgen}}, {{cog|en|worry}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈvʏrɡən/|[ˈvʏʁ.ɡŋ̍]|[ˈvʏɐ̯-]|[ˈʋ-]|[-ɡən]}}
* {{audio|de|De-würgen.ogg|Audio}}
* {{hyphenation|de|wür|gen}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[strangle]], [[choke]]
#: {{ux|de|Die Krawatte ist so eng, dass sie mich '''würgt'''.|The tie is so tight that it's '''choking''' me.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[gag]], [[retch]]
#: {{ux|de|Als er die Leiche sah, musste er '''würgen'''.|When he saw the corpse, he had to '''retch'''.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive|with {{m|de|an}} + dative}} to have trouble [[chew]]ing or [[swallow]]ing, to [[gag]] on
#: {{ux|de|Er '''würgte''' an einem allzu großen Bissen.|He '''gagged''' on an all too big bite.}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich wollte höflich sein, also '''würgte''' ich tapfer an dem zähen, versalzenen Fleisch.|I wanted to be polite, so I bravely '''tried to chew''' the sinewy, oversalted meat.}}

